Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:26:43 -0500
Subject: feat: the download toast's menu moves the file to the Trash (S-489)

A new download shows Chromium's bubble from the downloads button, the
toast Arc users know. Its row's menu opened the file or showed it in the
Finder, and nothing put the file in the Trash or took it off the list
without opening the Downloads panel. A finished download's menu there now
has the panel's own verbs (sidebar-panels Pn9, Pn11): Move to Trash (Move
to Recycle Bin on Windows), never deleted outright, after which the row
reads as removed; and Remove from List, where the profile may delete
history, which takes the download off the list and out of the history and
leaves the file.

The two are Stedding's ids outside DownloadCommands, so Chromium's
metrics of the menu stay as they were. Linux, not shipped, has no Trash of
Stedding's and offers Remove from List alone.

Why: GitHub discussion 116; the owner asked for the requests that could
ship in 0.5.1 (2026-11-14). Spec: sidebar-panels Pn19.
Removable when: never; Stedding's own verbs in a Chromium menu.
